          "responses": [
            {
              "feedback": {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Correct. No buffer can be present during the titration of a strong acid by a strong base, because no weak components are produced."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "c803ffe90d5041ecbe3f39de6571dc89",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1670046586"
              },
              "id": "3337503961",
              "legacyMatch": "ccfd7e32bcf34ffbb8942c1c4d5598fe",
              "rule": "input like {ccfd7e32bcf34ffbb8942c1c4d5598fe}",
              "score": 10
            },
            {
              "feedback": {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Remember that a buffer is present when a weak acid and its conjugate base (or weak base and its conjugate acid) are both present in significant amounts in the solution. For a titration involving a strong acid and strong base, there are no weak components that can produce a buffer system. For a titration involving a weak acid and strong base (or weak base and strong acid), the moles of the strong component react stoichiometrically with the weak acid (HA) or weak base (B), which neutralizes the weak component and converts the weak component into its conjugate base ("
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          }
                        ],
                        "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                        "src": "\\text A^-",
                        "subtype": "latex",
                        "type": "formula_inline"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ") or conjugate acid ("
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          }
                        ],
                        "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                        "src": "\\text{BH}^+",
                        "subtype": "latex",
                        "type": "formula_inline"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "). The buffer portion of the titration has significant amounts of both weak components ("
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          }
                        ],
                        "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                        "src": "\\text{HA}",
                        "subtype": "latex",
                        "type": "formula_inline"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " and "
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          }
                        ],
                        "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                        "src": "\\text A^-",
                        "subtype": "latex",
                        "type": "formula_inline"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ", or "
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          }
                        ],
                        "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                        "src": "\\text B",
                        "subtype": "latex",
                        "type": "formula_inline"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " and "
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          }
                        ],
                        "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                        "src": "\\text{BH}^+",
                        "subtype": "latex",
                        "type": "formula_inline"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ") and ideally equal concentrations of both components. Equal concentrations occur at the half-equivalence point, when the amount of strong component that has been added is equal to half of the weak component in the initial solution. At this point, half of the weak component (HA or B) is converted into its conjugate ("
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          }
                        ],
                        "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                        "src": "\\text A^-",
                        "subtype": "latex",
                        "type": "formula_inline"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " or "
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          }
                        ],
                        "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                        "src": "\\text{NH}^+",
                        "subtype": "latex",
                        "type": "formula_inline"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "), so that the solution contains equal amounts of both weak components."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "bc7d54f7584a49619e2a5ca2db6cabea",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
